/dist/
/ccdad
/ccdad.exe

# Claude Code's own files, anywhere in the tree. Nothing in this repository
# writes one: the suite points every path at a temp directory, and a relative
# store is refused outright. What did write them was a MUTATION run — a
# deliberately broken build resolving the global config to a relative path —
# and three reached a commit before a merge listing happened to name them.
# They are credential-shaped and this repository is public, so no arrangement
# of the tree makes one of them ours to track.
.claude.json
.credentials.json

# Claude Code's worktree scratch space. A subagent given an isolated checkout
# gets one here, and a run that dies before its cleanup leaves the directory
# behind — registered as a git worktree, so it shows up as untracked content in
# the main tree and lands in a `git add -A` if nobody is looking. Nothing in it
# is ours to track; `git worktree remove --force` is how one is cleared.
.claude/
